ubernetes APIServer                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                | `true`                           |","+| `multicluster.clusterGateway.replicaCount`                    | ClusterGateway replica count                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                               | `1`                              |","+| `multicluster.clusterGateway.port`                            | ClusterGateway port                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                        | `9443`                           |","+| `multicluster.clusterGateway.image.repository`                | ClusterGateway image repository                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                            | `oamdev/cluster-gateway`         |","+| `multicluster.clusterGateway.image.tag`                       | ClusterGateway image tag                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   | `v1.9.0-alpha.2`                 |","+| `multicluster.clusterGateway.image.pullPolicy`                | ClusterGateway image pull policy                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                           | `IfNotPresent`                   |","+| `multicluster.clusterGateway.resources.requests.cpu`          | ClusterGateway cpu request                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                 | `50m`                            |","+| `multicluster.clusterGateway.resources.requests.memory`       | ClusterGateway memory request                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                              | `20Mi`                           |","+| `multicluster.clusterGateway.resources.limits.cpu`            | ClusterGateway cpu limit                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   | `500m`                           |","+| `multicluster.clusterGateway.resources.limits.memory`         | ClusterGateway memory limit                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                | `200Mi`                          |","+| `multicluster.clusterGateway.secureTLS.enabled`               | Whether to enable secure TLS. When secure TLS and multicluster.enabled are on and cert-manager is off, the chart starts vela-core with --cluster-gateway-tls-secret, so vela-core generates the cluster-gateway serving cert at startup and sets the APIService caBundle when the APIService points at the chart's cluster-gateway Service | `true`                           |","+| `multicluster.clusterGateway.secureTLS.certPath`              | Path to the certificate file                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                               | `/etc/k8s-cluster-gateway-certs` |","+| `multicluster.clusterGateway.secureTLS.certManager.enabled`   | Whether to enable cert-manager                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                             | `false`                          |","+| `multicluster.clusterGateway.serviceMonitor.enabled`          | Whether to enable service monitor                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          | `false`                          |","+| `multicluster.clusterGateway.serviceMonitor.additionalLabels` | Additional labels for service monitor                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                      | `{}`                             |"," "," ### Test parameters"," "],"additions":19,"deletions":19,"truncated":false},{"path":"charts/vela-core/files/builtin-definitions/apply.sh","lines":["@@ -12,10 +12,13 @@ kubectl -n \"$CONTROLLER_NAMESPACE\" rollout status \"deployment/$CONTROLLER_DEPLOY"," "," # With cert-manager no hook patches the CA bundle in; its CA injector does, on"," # its own schedule. Until every webhook has one the API server cannot call them.","+# A webhook still waits while its caBundle is empty or the chart's Cg==","+# placeholder. A real bundle is base64 and can end in '=' padding, so the check","+# matches the whole value, not just a trailing '='."," if [ -n \"$WEBHOOK_CONFIGURATION\" ]; then","   waited=0","   while kubectl get validatingwebhookconfiguration \"$WEBHOOK_CONFIGURATION\" \\","-    -o jsonpath='{range .webhooks[*]}{.name}={.clientConfig.caBundle}{\"\\n\"}{end}' | grep -q '=$'; do","+    -o jsonpath='{range .webhooks[*]}{.name}={.clientConfig.caBundle}{\"\\n\"}{end}' | grep -qE '^[^=]+=(Cg==)?$'; do","     if [ \"$waited\" -ge \"$ROLLOUT_TIMEOUT_SECONDS\" ]; then","       echo \"Webhook $WEBHOOK_CONFIGURATION still has no CA bundle after ${waited}s\" >&2","       exit 1"],"additions":4,"deletions":1,"truncated":false},{"path":"charts/vela-core/templates/_helpers.tpl","lines":["@@ -136,3 +136,79 @@ of one kind. Takes a dict of \"kind\" and \"root\" (the chart context)."," {{- define \"kubevela.builtinDefinitionsConfigMap\" -}}"," {{- printf \"%s-builtin-%ss\" (include \"kubevela.fullname\" .root) (lower .kind) -}}"," {{- end -}}","+","+{{/*","+Returns \"true\" when vela-core manages the admission webhook serving cert","+itself (--webhook-tls-secret). The alternatives are cert-manager and a Secret","+that the user supplies.","+*/}}","+{{- define \"kubevela.webhookRuntimeCerts\" -}}","+{{- if and .Values.admissionWebhooks.enabled .Values.admissionWebhooks.patch.enabled (not .Values.admissionWebhooks.certManager.enabled) -}}true{{- end -}}","+{{- end -}}","+","+{{/*","+Returns \"true\" when the chart manages the cluster-gateway APIService: the","+APIService does not exist yet, or a Helm release created it. An APIService","+without Helm annotations belongs to an external controller, and the chart does","+not touch it.","+*/}}","+{{- define \"kubevela.clusterGatewayAPIServiceManaged\" -}}","+{{- $apiSvc := lookup \"apiregistration.k8s.io/v1\" \"APIService\" \"\" \"v1alpha1.cluster.core.oam.dev\" -}}","+{{- if or (not $apiSvc) (dig \"metadata\" \"annotations\" \"meta.helm.sh/release-name\" \"\" $apiSvc) -}}true{{- end -}}","+{{- end -}}","+","+{{/*","+Returns \"true\" when vela-core manages the cluster-gateway serving cert itself","+(--cluster-gateway-tls-secret). The alternative is cert-manager.","+*/}}","+{{- define \"kubevela.clusterGatewayRuntimeCerts\" -}}","+{{- if and .Values.multicluster.enabled .Values.multicluster.clusterGateway.secureTLS.enabled (not .Values.multicluster.clusterGateway.secureTLS.certManager.enabled) -}}true{{- end -}}","+{{- end -}}","+","+{{/*","+Returns the webhooks of an existing webhook configuration as JSON, keyed by","+webhook name. Takes a dict of \"kind\" and \"name\" (the configuration).","+*/}}","+{{- define \"kubevela.existingWebhooks\" -}}","+{{- $hooks := dict -}}","+{{- $existing := lookup \"admissionregistration.k8s.io/v1\" .kind \"\" .name -}}","+{{- if $existing -}}","+{{- range $existing.webhooks -}}{{- $_ := set $hooks .name . -}}{{- end -}}","+{{- end -}}","+{{- toJson $hooks -}}","+{{- end -}}","+","+{{/*","+Renders the caBundle line of one webhook. Takes a dict of \"root\", \"hooks\"","+(from kubevela.existingWebhooks) and \"name\" (the webhook). It keeps a valid","+caBundle that is already in the cluster, so that an upgrade does not break","+admission. When vela-core manages the cert, it renders no placeholder, because","+vela-core sets the caBundle at startup.","+*/}}","+{{- define \"kubevela.webhookCABundle\" -}}","+{{- $ca := dig .name \"clientConfig\" \"caBundle\" \"\" .hooks -}}","+{{- if include \"kubevela.webhookRuntimeCerts\" .root -}}","+{{- if and $ca (ne $ca \"Cg==\") }}caBundle: {{ $ca }}{{ end -}}","+{{- else -}}","+caBundle: {{ default \"Cg==\" $ca }}","+{{- end -}}","+{{- end -}}","+","+{{/*","+Renders the failurePolicy line of one webhook. Takes a dict of \"root\", \"hooks\",","+\"name\" and \"policy\". \"policy\" applies when the chart does not patch the","+webhooks. With patching on, webhooks start as Ignore until the caBundle is set.","+When vela-core manages the cert, vela-core then sets","+admissionWebhooks.failurePolicy. Thus the chart keeps the live policy on","+upgrade.","+*/}}","+{{- define \"kubevela.webhookFailurePolicy\" -}}","+{{- $live := dig .name \"failurePolicy\" \"\" .hooks -}}","+{{- if and (include \"kubevela.webhookRuntimeCerts\" .root) $live -}}","+failurePolicy: {{ $live }}","+{{- else if .root.Values.admissionWebhooks.patch.enabled -}}","+failurePolicy: Ignore","+{{- else -}}","+failurePolicy: {{ .policy }}","+{{- end -}}","+{{- end -}}"],"additions":76,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"charts/vela-core/templates/admission-webhooks/job-patch/clusterrole.yaml","lines":["@@ -1,28 +0,0 @@","-{{- if and .Values.admissionWebhooks.enabled .Values.admissionWebhooks.patch.enabled .Values.rbac.create (not .Values.admissionWebhooks.certManager.enabled) }}","-apiVersion: rbac.authorization.k8s.io/v1","-kind: ClusterRole","-metadata:","-  name:  {{ template \"kubevela.fullname\" . }}-admission","-  annotations:","-    \"helm.sh/hook\": pre-install,pre-upgrade,post-install,post-upgrade,post-rollback","-   